<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ApprovalProcess xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ApprovalProcess> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW 2026-08-28. Moves principal sign-off OFF Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval (now
        deactivated, see that file's own comment) and ONTO the Underwriting__c child record
        itself. User request: "We need the approval on Underwriting, not on Opportunity... if
        the underwriting is not approved, [Initiate LOI] will not move on to LOI." Full plan:
        agent-output/design-requirements.md.

        USER DECISIONS THIS FILE IS BUILT TO (do not re-open):
          D1 Approvers UNCHANGED - nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat + aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@
             avanzasolutions.com, whenMultipleApprovers = FirstResponse, allowDelegate false,
             allowRecall true.
          D2 REJECT HANDLING IS DROPPED. finalRejectionActions is intentionally ABSENT below -
             not an oversight. Stage__c never changes on rejection (entry criterion is
             Stage__c = 'In Progress' and nothing moves it during the pending window, so a
             Stage__c-keyed automation could not see a rejection even if one were added). On
             rejection the record simply stays at Stage__c = 'In Progress' / Status__c =
             'In Progress' and ONLY the approval history records the decision.
             🔴 ACCEPTED, DOCUMENTED REGRESSION: Opportunity.Underwriting_Complete__c is no
             longer cleared on reject the way today's (now-inert) UW_Reopen_For_Revision field
             update did. Nothing on this object replaces that behaviour. If the analyst needs
             to rework a rejected underwriting, they edit the record directly (it unlocks on
             rejection under recordEditability = AdminOnly) - there is no automated re-open.
          D3 recordEditability = AdminOnly - the Underwriting record LOCKS while pending.
          D4 Opportunity.UW_Approved__c / Underwriting_Status__c / Underwriting_Complete__c
             mirror fields are KEPT and must keep working - done by
             flows/Underwriting_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml calling
             UnderwritingApprovalStampService in ONE parent DML (see that flow's own header).

        🔴 finalApprovalActions WRITE ONLY THIS RECORD'S OWN FIELDS (Stage__c, Status__c). An
        approval process can field-update ONLY its own record or a MASTER-DETAIL parent, and
        Underwriting__c.Opportunity__c is a LOOKUP (fields/Opportunity__c.field-meta.xml,
        deleteConstraint SetNull) - so this process structurally CANNOT touch the Opportunity.
        The parent mirror write is therefore a separate, decoupled step: the after-save flow
        named above, entry-scoped on Stage__c changing TO 'Approved', calling
        UnderwritingApprovalStampService(underwritingId). That flow is a SEPARATE deploy unit
        from this one; nothing in this file depends on it existing for THIS record's own
        Stage__c / Status__c to update correctly.

        approvalPageFields DROP Asking_Price__c and Underwriting_Notes__c (Opportunity fields;
        Underwriting__c has no counterpart for either - confirmed against
        objects/Underwriting__c/fields/, 18 fields, no notes field, no asking price). Approvers
        who need deal-level context (asking price, underwriting notes) open the parent deal via
        the Opportunity__c lookup shown on the approval page. User-decision GATE B in the design
        doc; not invented here.

        entryCriteria is Stage__c = 'In Progress' ONLY - matching
        Underwriting__c.Submit_for_Approval's own visibility rule on
        flexipages/Underwriting_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml (pure "1 AND 2": custom
        permission AND Stage__c = 'In Progress'), so the quick action and the approval's entry
        criterion agree by construction.

        recordEditability = AdminOnly LOCKS THIS UNDERWRITING RECORD, NOT THE PARENT DEAL. The
        Opportunity is correctly editable throughout - Amount / Asking_Price__c etc. are NOT
        locked by this approval (verify: N-5 in the design doc's post-deploy checklist).

        🔴 RECALL ROUTE IS A SEPARATE, MANDATORY DEPLOY. With recordEditability = AdminOnly, a
        submitted record with no Recall route is a trap. See
        layouts/Underwriting__c-Underwriting Layout.layout-meta.xml (RelatedProcessHistoryList)
        AND flexipages/Underwriting_Record_Page.flexipage-meta.xml (force:relatedListContainer)
        - TWO FILES, NEITHER WORKS ALONE (measured on Disposition_Record_Page /
        Disposition__c-Disposition Layout: force:relatedListSingleContainer returns INVALID_TYPE
        for approval history; only force:relatedListContainer renders it). Both ship in the same
        change as this file.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. workflows/Underwriting__c.workflow-meta.xml (the two field
        updates referenced below) must land BEFORE this file, same requirement as
        Disposition_Offer__c.Offer_Selection_Approval / workflows/Disposition_Offer__c.
        Sequencing against the Opportunity-side retirement (deactivate old approval -> rewrite
        Underwriting_Approved_Before_LOI -> activate this process) is a devops/deployment-order
        decision, not encoded in this file's <active> value; see
        agent-output/design-requirements.md section 3 for the reasoning if deployed in separate
        passes rather than one atomic deploy.

        🔴 ONE PENDING ProcessInstance EXISTS TODAY ON THE OLD Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval
        (verified live 2026-08-28: ProcessInstance Id 04giw0000003C9VAAU, TargetObjectId
        006iw000000c3OHAAY, Status = Pending). It must be RECALLED IN SETUP before this change
        deploys - see approvalProcesses/Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval.approvalProcess-
        meta.xml for the full flag. Not actioned by this agent.

        NAMING - agent-output/design-requirements.md section 10 left these open; chosen here:
        process label "Underwriting Approval" (fullName Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval -
        distinct from the retired Opportunity.Underwriting_Approval, different object, no
        collision), step label "Principal approves underwriting" (not the shared "Principal
        Review" every other approval used before the 2026-08-26 disposition rename - approvers
        must be able to tell which request they are looking at), own-record field updates
        UW_Stage_Approved / UW_Status_Approved.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <allowRecall>true</allowRecall>
    <allowedSubmitters>
        <type>owner</type>
    </allowedSubmitters>
    <approvalPageFields>
        <field>Name</field>
        <field>Owner</field>
        <field>Opportunity__c</field>
        <field>My_Price__c</field>
        <field>My_Cap_Rate__c</field>
        <field>Market_Cap_Rate__c</field>
        <field>Underwritten_NOI__c</field>
        <field>Target_Return__c</field>
        <field>Principal_Price_Decision__c</field>
        <field>Stage__c</field>
    </approvalPageFields>
    <approvalStep>
        <allowDelegate>false</allowDelegate>
        <assignedApprover>
            <approver>
                <name>nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <approver>
                <name>aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@avanzasolutions.com</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <whenMultipleApprovers>FirstResponse</whenMultipleApprovers>
        </assignedApprover>
        <label>Principal approves underwriting</label>
        <name>Principal_Review_Step</name>
    </approvalStep>
    <description>Principal decision to approve this deal underwriting. Entry: Stage equals In Progress. Approval sets Stage to Approved and Status to Approved by Principals; a flow mirrors approval onto the Opportunity. Rejection returns to In Progress for rework.</description>
    <enableMobileDeviceAccess>false</enableMobileDeviceAccess>
    <entryCriteria>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Underwriting__c.Stage__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>In Progress</value>
        </criteriaItems>
    </entryCriteria>
    <finalApprovalActions>
        <action>
            <name>UW_Stage_Approved</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
        <action>
            <name>UW_Status_Approved</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalApprovalActions>
    <finalApprovalRecordLock>false</finalApprovalRecordLock>
    <finalRejectionRecordLock>false</finalRejectionRecordLock>
    <label>Underwriting Approval</label>
    <processOrder>1</processOrder>
    <recordEditability>AdminOnly</recordEditability>
    <showApprovalHistory>true</showApprovalHistory>
</ApprovalProcess>
